    "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\nRemove `/usr/local/cuda-*/NsightSystems-cli-*/target-linux-x64/plugins/efa_metrics/` at the end of the dev Docker image’s `main` stage to address `CVE-2026-27143`. The cleanup runs as root after the expensive dependency builds, preserving reuse of their cached layers. The `jet` stage inherits the cleaned `main` image. The glob covers installed CUDA and Nsight Systems versions, and `rm -rf` succeeds when the plugin is absent.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Passed a focused Docker build running the cleanup against the pinned `nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:26.08-py3` base: removed both matching paths, preserved all 42 neighboring plugin paths, and repeated the cleanup successfully.\n- Passed temporary filesystem checks for absent paths, multiple CUDA/Nsight versions, a CUDA symlink alias, and preservation of unrelated plugins and the ARM64 plugin path.\n- Verified that the diff from the PR base contains only the final cleanup insertion: all earlier Dockerfile instructions remain unchanged, cleanup runs as root, and `jet` inherits it.\n- Passed shell syntax checks for the standalone cleanup and all Dockerfile Bash heredocs, plus `git diff --check`.\n- Passed `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` (no changed Python files).\n- Full dependency image build and GPU tests were not run.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Ran the repository autoformatter in check mode.\n- Unit tests, functional tests, typing, and documentation changes are not applicable to this Docker cleanup.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
